{
  "dom_id": "step-q36698",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+1 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}+2 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Approaching $x=0$ from the left, we have $x<0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={e}^{x}+1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}({e}^{x}+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe right-sided limit ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (0,1).$ \n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=2,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
      "choices": [
